ype">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Annals and Antiquities of Rajasthan is a history of the Rajput states by James Tod, published in two volumes in London in 1829 and 1832.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-inisfallen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annals-of-inisfallen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annals of Inisfallen</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Annals of Inisfallen are a chronicle of medieval Irish history, preserved in a manuscript written largely in the late 11th century and continued by later hands into…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-loch-ce"><span class="enc-name">Annals of Loch Cé</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Annals of Loch Cé are an Irish chronicle in Irish and Latin covering events from 1014 to 1590, chiefly in Connacht.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-the-joseon-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annals-of-the-joseon-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annals of the Joseon Dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Annals of the Joseon Dynasty (Joseon Wangjo Sillok) are the official chronicles of the reigns of Joseon kings from Taejo to Cheoljong, covering 1392 to 1863 in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-the-kaqchikels"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annals-of-the-kaqchikels.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annals of the Kaqchikels</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Annals of the Kaqchikels is a chronicle written in the Kaqchikel Maya language in Latin script by members of the Xajil family in the late 16th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-ulster"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annals-of-ulster.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annals of Ulster</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Annals of Ulster are a chronicle of Irish history from the fifth century to the sixteenth, compiled in the late fifteenth century for Cathal Óg Mac Maghnusa on…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annaly"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annaly.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annaly</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Annaly was a medieval Irish lordship in the northern part of Tethba, roughly the area of modern County Longford.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/annama-deva"><span class="enc-name">Annama Deva</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Annama Deva is the traditional founder of the Kakatiya royal line of Bastar in central India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/annapolis-royal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/annapolis-royal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Annapolis Royal</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Annapolis Royal is a town on the Annapolis Basin in western Nova Scotia, Canada.</span></a></li></ul>
